#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:6
msgid "# Unified Recall Retrieval and Loading Flow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:9
msgid ""
"> **v1 ✅ Implemented:** `memory_recall(query)` four-source unified recall + "
"RRF reranking, returns `results[]` (distinguished by `memory_type`); session "
"hits are snippets ([`life/memory/src/recall-search.ts`](../../life/memory/"
"src/recall-search.ts)).  > **v2 target design** (not implemented): resource "
"layer + preset + lean index loading chain, see [Issue #47](https://"
"github.com/freeanima-org/freeanima/issues/47)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:11
msgid "## v1 Implemented"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Capability        | Description                                                                                  |\n"
"| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `memory_recall`   | Four sources: semantic / session / limbic / autobiographical; Top N; session returns snippet |\n"
"| `sessions_search` | Session message FTS; returns snippet (not full content)                                      |\n"
"| `memory_remember` | semantic_memory CRUD                                                                         |\n"
"| Resident memory   | system prompt injection (not recall)                                                         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:20
msgid "## v2 Target Design (Issue #47)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:22
msgid "> The following is v2 design draft, **not current runtime behavior**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:26
msgid ""
"**`recall` retrieves only, does not load.** Returns lean index (title + "
"description + type + id), not full content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:26
msgid ""
"**Scope: memory layer + resource layer.** Self layer always injected in "
"system prompt, outside recall scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:26
msgid ""
"**Loading handled by downstream tools.** recall tells the LLM \"what "
"exists\"; LLM decides \"what to fetch\", then calls corresponding load tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:28
msgid "## Retrieval Scope (v2 Design)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"recall unified retrieval\n"
"├── Memory Layer\n"
"│   ├── Semantic memory — semantic_memory (world/experience/opinion/…)\n"
"│   ├── Episodic memory — messages (conversation FTS)\n"
"│   ├── Procedural memory — skills / procedural facts\n"
"│   └── Limbic memory — imprint (semantic_memory); limbic table (✅ implemented, light sleep Phase 2 writes, not via recall)\n"
"│\n"
"└── Resource Layer (Estate Layer, v2 design)\n"
"    ├── Tools\n"
"    ├── Skills\n"
"    ├── Internal assets (notes, projects, code, docs)\n"
"    └── Entity graph\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:45
msgid "### Out of Retrieval Scope"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Content                     | Reason                  | Access                                                   |\n"
"| --------------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Self layer six blocks       | Small, always needed    | Always injected in system prompt                         |\n"
"| Full tool schemas           | Needed only before call | `load_tools` (v2) / existing `reload_tools`              |\n"
"| Full memory detail          | Needed on demand        | `read_memory` (v2) / existing `remember` single-row read |\n"
"| Full file content           | Needed on demand        | `read_file` ✅                                           |\n"
"| Entity relationship network | Traverse on demand      | `graph_query` (v2)                                       |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:55
msgid "## Presets (v2 Design)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:57
msgid ""
"`recall` uses `preset` parameter to steer search direction. Presets are "
"**weighting templates** over memory/resource types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:59
msgid "### Preset Definitions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Preset               | Semantic | Episodic | Limbic | Procedural | Skills | Tools | Notes                              |\n"
"| -------------------- | -------- | -------- | ------ | ---------- | ------ | ----- | ---------------------------------- |\n"
"| `balanced` (default) | Med      | Med      | Low    | Med        | Med    | Low   | General, no bias                   |\n"
"| `recall`             | High     | High     | High   | Low        | Low    | —     | Remember past, recover emotion     |\n"
"| `work`               | Low      | —        | —      | High       | High   | High  | Complete tasks, solve problems     |\n"
"| `debug`              | Med      | Med      | —      | High       | High   | High  | Troubleshoot, needs tech + context |\n"
"| `learn`              | High     | Low      | —      | High       | Med    | Low   | Understand a concept or domain     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:69
msgid "### Extensibility"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:71
msgid ""
"Presets are templates, not fixed taxonomy. New presets later (e.g. `social`, "
"`create`). Default `balanced` when preset omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:73
msgid "### Usage Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"recall(\"how to query database\", preset=\"work\")\n"
"→ procedural memory +++\n"
"→ skills      +++\n"
"→ tools       +++\n"
"→ semantic    +\n"
"→ episodic    - (almost none)\n"
"→ limbic      -- (hardly needed)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"recall(\"that database issue we discussed last time\", preset=\"recall\")\n"
"→ episodic    +++\n"
"→ limbic      +++\n"
"→ semantic    ++\n"
"→ procedural  +\n"
"→ skills      -\n"
"→ tools       -- (hardly needed)\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:93
msgid "## Full Flow (v2 Design)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"Partner question / LLM needs information\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼\n"
"① recall(query, preset=\"...\")\n"
"   └── Unified search memory layer + resource layer\n"
"   └── Return lean result list (title + description + type + id)\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼  LLM decides what is needed and how to use it\n"
"        │\n"
"② Choose downstream load tool by result type:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   ┌──────────────┬──────────────────────────┐\n"
"   │ Result type  │ Downstream load tool     │\n"
"   ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────┤\n"
"   │ Tool         │ load_tools([\"name\"])     │ → full schema\n"
"   │ Skill        │ load_skill(\"name\")       │ → injectable skill\n"
"   │ Semantic/limbic memory │ read_memory(\"semantic_memory_id\") │ → full fact content\n"
"   │ Episodic snippet │ scroll_session(\"id\") │ → recent conversation context\n"
"   │ File/doc     │ read_file(\"path\")        │ → file content\n"
"   │ Entity graph │ graph_query(\"entity\")    │ → related network\n"
"   └──────────────┴──────────────────────────┘\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼\n"
"③ LLM responds or decides further based on loaded content\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:122 docs/concepts/time-perception.md:54
msgid "### Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:125
msgid "``` You: Check on the server whether Nginx logs have recent errors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"① I → recall(\"nginx logs server errors\", preset=\"work\")\n"
"    Returns:\n"
"    - Tool: tail_logs - view tail of file\n"
"    - Tool: grep_logs - search logs for keyword\n"
"    - Fact: Nginx logs at /var/log/nginx/access.log\n"
"    - Skill: Standard Nginx error troubleshooting flow\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"② I need tools → load_tools([\"tail_logs\", \"grep_logs\"])\n"
"    Returns full schema:\n"
"    tail_logs(path, lines)\n"
"    grep_logs(path, pattern)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"③ I call tail_logs(path=\"/var/log/nginx/access.log\", lines=50)\n"
"    grep_logs(path=\"/var/log/nginx/error.log\", pattern=\"5xx\")\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:143
msgid "## Relationship to Self Layer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:145
msgid "Self layer (six blocks) is not retrieved via `recall`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:151
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer          | Injection                  | Reason                                                |\n"
"| -------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Self layer     | Always in system prompt    | Small, fixed, every conversation needs \"who I am\"     |\n"
"| Memory layer   | `recall` + downstream load | Large, dynamic, search on demand                      |\n"
"| Resource layer | `recall` + downstream load | Tool definitions needed temporarily, load before call |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:153
msgid "## Naming Rationale"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:155
msgid "The name `recall` stays unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:157
msgid ""
"In cognitive psychology, Recall is the standard term for actively pulling "
"stored information from memory—no external cue, no prompt, you \"remember\" "
"yourself. This is not exploring the unknown (discover/find), but retrieving "
"what you already stored. Even when scope extends from memory layer to "
"resource layer, the action's essence is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:159 docs/concepts/self-layer.md:108
msgid "## Design Evolution"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/recall-flow.md:167
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"v1 (✅ current): recall searches semantic_memory + messages FTS, returns JSON structured results\n"
"v2 (design #47): recall unified search memory layer + resource layer\n"
"            └── introduce preset\n"
"            └── introduce downstream load chain (load_tools / read_memory etc.)\n"
"v3 (future): TBD\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

